# SOURCE: bin/claude_launch.identity
# STATUS: PROD — vendor identity of the co-located N1 launcher (claude_launch.sh)
#
# Pure vendor fact: the name + email used for the git CO-AUTHOR attribution when publishing to GitHub.
# Never read by the pod: `bin/publish-transform.sh` sources it, run host-side by the runtime's
# publish rail (MCP `project_publish`) or by the operator. The co-author IS THE VENDOR, never hardcoded in the publication
# logic: each vendor carries ITS OWN identity, co-located with ITS launcher, the same discipline as the
# N0/N1 frontier ("new vendor → new bin/<vendor>_launch.sh" — here: "→ co-locate
# bin/<vendor>_launch.identity").
#
# On the work forge the real role is the `Co-authored-by: LCARS-<role>` trailer (Fleet.Credentials.
# ForgeIdentity, commit gate). THIS file concerns ONLY the rewrite at GitHub publish time: the internal
# role disappears and only the vendor that did the work stays credited (with the human as author).

NAME="Claude"
EMAIL="noreply@anthropic.com"
